- Select customer or walk-in customer.
- Add multiple products.
- Enter quantities.
- Apply permitted discounts.
- Configure applicable tax fields.
- Calculate line totals and invoice totals.
- Select payment method.
- Support paid, partially paid, and unpaid sales.
- Add notes.
- Preview invoice before saving.

Invoice features:
- Generate a unique invoice number within the business.
- Generate printable and downloadable PDF invoices.
- Include business details, customer details, item descriptions, quantities, prices, discounts, tax breakdown, totals, and payment status.
- Support A4 and compact invoice layouts where practical.
- Reprint existing invoices without changing their financial data.
- Search, filter, paginate, and export sales records.

Critical requirements:
- Recalculate all totals on the server.
- Never trust frontend-supplied prices, taxes, discounts, or totals.
- Use decimal-safe monetary calculations, such as integer minor currency units or a suitable decimal library.
- Use transaction-safe invoice number allocation.
- Avoid duplicate invoices during retries.
- Update stock and create stock movements atomically with the sale.
- Record payments as separate transactions.
- Support controlled cancellation and refund workflows.
- Preserve historical invoice snapshots when products or customer details change.
- Use database transactions when supported by the deployed database configuration.
- Implement idempotency for sale creation where appropriate.

Tax and compliance:
- Support configurable tax rates and tax breakdowns.
- Treat GST settings as configurable business data.
- Do not claim that generated invoices are legally GST-compliant in every situation.
- Validate statutory requirements with a qualified professional before marketing compliance features.

